  <!-- ITEM 18: DEFINITION OF EXTENSIVELY DRUG-RESISTANT TB (XDR-TB) -->
  <div class="question-card">
    <div class="meta-bar">
      <span>Question 18</span>
      <span>Category: Pharmacology & Tuberculosis</span>
    </div>
    <div class="vignette">
      A 48-year-old male immigrant from an area with high prevalence of refractory tuberculosis is admitted with persistent cavitary pulmonary disease despite compliance with multiple antitubercular courses. Sputum cultures grow <em>Mycobacterium tuberculosis</em>. Drug susceptibility testing confirms resistance to isoniazid, rifampicin, levofloxacin, and amikacin.
    </div>
    <div class="stem">
      According to World Health Organization criteria detailed in the pharmacology course, which of the following categories correctly classifies this mycobacterial strain?
    </div>
    <ul class="options">
      <li><strong>A.</strong> Monoresistant tuberculosis</li>
      <li><strong>B.</strong> Polyresistant tuberculosis</li>
      <li><strong>C.</strong> Multidrug-resistant tuberculosis (MDR-TB)</li>
      <li><strong>D.</strong> Extensively drug-resistant tuberculosis (XDR-TB)</li>
      <li><strong>E.</strong> Pan-susceptible tuberculosis</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="explanation">
      <div class="correct-badge">Correct Answer: D</div>
      <div class="rationale">
        By definition, <strong>Multidrug-Resistant TB (MDR-TB)</strong> refers to resistance to at least <strong>both Isoniazid and Rifampicin</strong>. <strong>Extensively Drug-Resistant TB (XDR-TB)</strong> is defined as MDR-TB (resistant to both isoniazid and rifampicin) plus resistance to <strong>any fluoroquinolone</strong> (e.g., levofloxacin or moxifloxacin) AND at least <strong>one second-line injectable agent</strong> (e.g., amikacin, capreomycin, or kanamycin) or bedaquiline/linezolid in updated WHO definitions.
      </div>
      <div class="distractors">
        <strong>Distractor Breakdown:</strong>
        <ul>
          <li><em>Option A:</em> Monoresistant TB is resistance to only one first-line drug.</li>
          <li><em>Option B:</em> Polyresistant TB is resistance to two or more first-line drugs, but not to both isoniazid and rifampicin together.</li>
          <li><em>Option C:</em> MDR-TB is resistant to isoniazid and rifampicin, but retains susceptibility to fluoroquinolones and second-line injectables.</li>
          <li><em>Option E:</em> Pan-susceptible implies full susceptibility to all first-line agents.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="citation">Source: Treatment of Tuberculosis.pptx &amp; Final Exam Recall Item 82</div>
    </div>
