  <!-- ITEM 19: CEFTRIAXONE BILIARY EXCRETION -->
  <div class="question-card">
    <div class="meta-bar">
      <span>Question 19</span>
      <span>Category: Antimicrobial Pharmacokinetics</span>
    </div>
    <div class="vignette">
      An 81-year-old female with severe chronic kidney disease (baseline estimated GFR 18 mL/min/1.73m²) is admitted to the hospital with acute community-acquired lobar pneumonia. Empiric therapy requires an intravenous third-generation cephalosporin active against <em>Streptococcus pneumoniae</em>.
